    "value": "This page tracks one-time **CI/CD and environment infrastructure** setup tasks — distinct from [7.1a Tool Access Tracker](https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/SFCC/pages/259686402) (per-person access) and [7.1b Third Party Credentials](https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/SFCC/pages/268337165) (vendor business credentials). Items marked ✅ are confirmed; ⬜ are open.\n\nRepository & Governance\n-----------------------\n\n| Task | Status | Owner | Notes |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| `AGENTS.md` + `CLAUDE.md` stub in place | ✅ | Tech Lead | Repo root |\n| `.claude/settings.json` with branch lock + permission allowlist | ✅ | Tech Lead |  |\n| `.claude/rules/` — frozen, protected, squad-a, squad-b, conventions | ✅ | Tech Lead + Squad Leads |  |\n| `.claude/skills/` — Claude Code skills | ✅ | Tech Lead | See [Claude Code Skills Reference](https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/SFCC/pages/297959425) |\n| `.claude/hooks/` — `tier2Warn`, `contentfulDriftWarn`, `testFileRemind` | ✅ | Tech Lead |  |\n| `CODEOWNERS` at repo root | ✅ | Tech Lead + Squad Leads |  |\n| Git hooks installed via Husky (`pre-commit`, `commit-msg`) | ✅ | Tech Lead | Auto-installs on `npm install` |\n| Cross-AI rules sync script | ✅ | Tech Lead | `npm run sync:ai-rules` |\n\nTest & QA\n---------\n\n| Task | Status | Owner | Notes |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| Confirm Jira project key prefix | ⬜ | Project Lead | Needed for `.feature` file naming and Zephyr traceability tags. Placeholder: `ZIM`. |\n| Confirm BrowserStack account exists | ⬜ | DevOps / Delivery Lead | Set `BROWSERSTACK_USERNAME` and `BROWSERSTACK_ACCESS_KEY` in GitHub Secrets, plus `RETAIL_APP_HOME_SIT`, `PWA_E2E_USER_EMAIL`, `PWA_E2E_USER_PASSWORD`, and `E2E_*` product SKU secrets. |\n| Confirm test management tool (Zephyr Scale, Zephyr Squad, or other) | ⬜ | QA Lead | Affects BrowserStack Test Observability → Zephyr sync config |\n| Set Playwright HTML report publishing | ⬜ | DevOps | Enable GitHub Pages → source: GitHub Actions (Settings → Pages) |\n\nCI/CD & Quality Gates\n---------------------\n\n| Task | Status | Owner | Notes |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| `digital-sit.yml`, `qa.yml`, `protected-file-guard.yml`, `upstream-release-watch.yml`, `weekly-agents.yml` ported | ✅ | Tech Lead | See the [PWA CI/CD Pipeline (GitHub Actions)](https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/SFCC/pages/305561601) page |\n| Configure `release/**` branch protection | ⬜ | Integration Lead | Required status check: `Digital SIT Gate` |\n| Set `LHCI_SERVER_BASE_URL` secret | ⬜ | Zimmermann IT / Accenture DevOps | Lighthouse CI trend storage |\n| Set `LHCI_TOKEN` secret | ⬜ | Zimmermann IT / Accenture DevOps | Lighthouse CI server auth |\n| Set `LHCI_TARGET_URL_SIT` secret | ⬜ | Accenture DevOps | SIT environment URL for Lighthouse runs |\n| Confirm MuleSoft contract endpoint | ⬜ | Integration Lead + Zimmermann integration team | The `test:contracts` script is a placeholder — must be replaced with a real Pact/OpenAPI assertion. This is the same OpenAPI spec dependency tracked on [7.1b Third Party Credentials](https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/SFCC/pages/268337165) (MuleSoft row) — don't track it twice, update status there. |\n\nSIT Environment\n---------------\n\n| Task | Status | Owner | Notes |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| Set `COMMERCE_API_CLIENT_ID_SIT` secret | ⬜ | Integration Lead | SFCC client ID for SIT org |\n| Set `COMMERCE_API_ORG_ID_SIT` secret | ⬜ | Integration Lead | SFCC org ID for SIT |\n| Set `COMMERCE_API_SHORT_CODE_SIT` secret | ⬜ | Integration Lead | SFCC short code for SIT |\n| Set `COMMERCE_API_SITE_ID_SIT` secret | ⬜ | Integration Lead | SFCC site ID for SIT instance |\n| Set `MRT_USER` secret | ⬜ | Accenture DevOps | MRT push / activate auth (shared with Digital Dev) |\n| Set `MRT_API_KEY` secret | ⬜ | Accenture DevOps | MRT push / activate auth (shared with Digital Dev) |\n| Confirm `SIT_URL` and set `MRT_SIT_URL` | ⬜ | Integration Lead | Used by the repo's `scripts/healthCheckAll.sh` |\n| Confirm MRT project slug and update `mobify.config.js` | ⬜ | Integration Lead | Placeholder — must be confirmed before deploy |\n| Create `sit` environment in GitHub repo | ⬜ | Accenture DevOps | Settings → Environments → New environment: `sit`. Required for the `deploy-sit` CI job. |\n\nMulti-site Configuration\n------------------------\n\n| Task | Status | Owner | Notes |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| Customise `config/sites.js` for the Zimmermann storefront set (7 sites: AU, UK, US, EU domestic, EU international, HK, ME) | ⬜ | Integration Lead | Currently OOTB Salesforce default. Must be customised before E2E fixtures keyed by `SITE_ID` can run. |\n| US storefront decision (REG-005) | ✅ | Project Lead + Integration Lead | Confirmed 2026-06-11: single US SFCC site. Domestic checkout = SFCC; international shipping = Global-e. |\n\nUpstream Sync\n-------------\n\n| Task | Status | Owner | Notes |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| Upstream baseline tracked | ✅ | Tech Lead | Current: `10.0.0` |\n\n---\n\nGitHub Branch Protection & CODEOWNERS Setup (one-time, ~15 minutes)\n-------------------------------------------------------------------\n\nDo this once when the repo is set up. The `protected-file-guard.yml` workflow and `CODEOWNERS` file do the detection — branch protection rules make them unmergeable when they fail.\n\n### 1. Protect `develop`\n\nSettings → Branches → Add branch protection rule → branch name pattern `develop`:\n\n| Setting | Value | Why |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| Require a pull request before merging | ✅ On | No direct pushes to develop |\n| Required approvals | **2** | One from owning squad, one cross-squad check |\n| Dismiss stale reviews when new commits are pushed | ✅ On | Forces re-review after changes |\n| Require review from Code Owners | ✅ On | Enforces CODEOWNERS — owner must approve |\n| Require status checks to pass before merging | ✅ On | Blocks merge if Actions fail |\n| Required status checks | `🔴 Tier 1 — Frozen Files Check`, `🔴 Branch Target Check`, `🟡 Tier 2 — Protected Files Warning`, `🟡 Cross-Squad Boundary Check` | All four required |\n| Require branches to be up to date before merging | ✅ On | Forces rebase on stale branches |\n| Do not allow bypassing the above settings | ✅ On | **Admins cannot bypass — critical** |\n\n### 2. Protect `main`\n\nSame pattern as `develop`, plus: Required approvals **2** (both squad leads), Restrict who can push (Integration Lead + Squad Leads only), Do not allow bypassing.\n\n### 3. Protect `release/*`\n\nRequired approvals **1**, require status checks to pass, restrict who can create matching branches to Squad Leads only.\n\n### 4. Status check names\n\nAfter the Actions workflow has run once, GitHub recognises the job names as available status checks. Exact strings to add:\n\nDefaultnone🔴 Tier 1 — Frozen Files Check\n🔴 Branch Target Check\n🟡 Tier 2 — Protected Files Warning\n🟡 Cross-Squad Boundary Check\n\n### 5. Create GitHub Teams (required for CODEOWNERS)\n\nOrg → Teams → New Team:\n\n| Team name | Slug | Members |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| Design System | `design-system` | UI Designer |\n| Integration Lead | `integration-lead` | SI Partner lead(s) |\n| Squad A Lead | `squad-a-lead` | Squad A tech lead |\n| Squad B Lead | `squad-b-lead` | Squad B tech lead |\n| Squad Leads | `squad-leads` | Both squad tech leads |\n\nThen update `CODEOWNERS`, replacing all `@your-org/` prefixes with the actual GitHub organisation slug.\n\n### 6. Install CodeRabbit\n\nSign up at coderabbit.ai with the GitHub org account, install the CodeRabbit GitHub App on the repo — `coderabbit.yaml` at the repo root is picked up automatically. No additional GitHub Actions setup needed.\n\n### 7. Verify everything is working\n\nOpen a test PR that targets `develop` and modifies one Tier 1 file. Expected: `🔴 Tier 1 — Frozen Files Check` fails with the owner contact message, other checks pass, CodeRabbit posts its review, the Integration Lead is auto-requested as reviewer, and the Merge button is blocked.\n\n### What this gives you — summary\n\n| Protection | Mechanism | Blocks Merge? |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| Tier 1 file touched | GitHub Action (tier1-guard) | ✅ Yes — hard fail |\n| Wrong branch target | GitHub Action (branch-target-guard) | ✅ Yes — hard fail |\n| Tier 2 file touched | GitHub Action (tier2-warning) + PR comment | ❌ No — warning only |\n| Cross-squad PR | GitHub Action (cross-squad-guard) + PR comment | ❌ No — warning only |\n| Tier 1 owner must approve | CODEOWNERS + branch protection | ✅ Yes — required review |\n| Tier 2 owner must approve | CODEOWNERS + branch protection | ✅ Yes — required review |\n| Code quality & SSR safety | CodeRabbit path\\_instructions | Via request\\_changes |\n| Secrets in code | CodeRabbit (gitleaks) | Via request\\_changes |\n| Chakra theme token violations | CodeRabbit custom\\_instructions | Via request\\_changes |\n| Missing Einstein events | CodeRabbit custom\\_instructions | Via request\\_changes |\n| Claude Code scope creep | CodeRabbit custom\\_instructions | Via request\\_changes |\n\n---\n\nPer-developer setup (tracked separately): see the [Technical Environment Setup](https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/SFCC/pages/304906242) page."
